OL,3,AAustralian shark attack victim grateful
OL,4,Afor 'second chance at life'
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn Australian woman bitten by a shark
OL,7,Fat a popular Sydney beach earlier this
OL,8,Fyear says she has been given a "second
OL,9,Fchance at life" and will be making the
OL,10,Fmost of it.
OL,12,FLeah Stewart, 35, was mauled by a shark
OL,13,Fduring a morning swim at Coogee Beach
OL,14,Fin June, suffering multiple bites to
OL,15,Fher arms and legs, amid a spate of
OL,16,Fattacks in Australia.
OL,18,FThe mother-of-one was placed in an
OL,19,Finduced coma and had several surgeries,
OL,20,Fincluding having one of her arms
OL,21,Famputated.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,0,100
